Removes RTCFileLogger and the File Timestamp privacy-manifest entry, and
fixes the macOS manifest path. Applies to webrtc-sdk/webrtc at ba469aa2,
after apple_prefix.patch.

Why: in the published LiveKitWebRTC framework the only stat-family import is
_stat, reached solely through RTCFileLogger -> FileRotatingLogSink ->
FileRotatingStream (IsFile, GetSize), found with ld -why_live,_stat on a
stock build. stat is in Apple's File Timestamp required-reason category.
Upstream tracks making RTCFileLogger optional as bugs.webrtc.org/337909152.

1. sdk/BUILD.gn: drop RTCFileLogger (header and file_logger_objc) from both
   framework bundles, and the unused file_logger_objc dependency of
   peerconnectionfactory_base_objc (with -all_load it would pull the class in).
2. tools_webrtc/apple/generate_privacy_manifest.py: drop the File Timestamp
   (C617.1) entry, which existed only for RTCFileLogger. System Boot Time
   (35F9.1, 8FFB.1) stays: mach_absolute_time is still used.
3. webrtc.gni: put the manifest at {{bundle_resources_dir}}. On macOS
   {{bundle_contents_dir}} is already Versions/A, so the old path produced
   Versions/A/Versions/A/Resources, where Apple's tools do not look.

